From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pwm: sun8i: Count the extra cycle when reading the period
 back

PPR.PWM_ENTIRE_CYCLE holds the number of cycles of a period minus one,
and sun8i_pwm_apply() programs it that way. sun8i_pwm_get_state() takes
the field as the number of cycles.

Without this, get_state() reports a period one cycle shorter than
apply() programmed, so applying the read-back state shortens the period
by one cycle each time; with CONFIG_PWM_DEBUG the core reports that
.apply is not idempotent.

Add the cycle in get_state(). The product in the period calculation
stays below 2^63: 0x10000 cycles, a prescaler of at most 0x100 and a
divider of at most 2^8 give 2^32, times 10^9.

Seen on the Radxa Cubie A7S.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board with CONFIG_PWM_DEBUG; a
period set on a PWM1 channel reads back as set, and the core no longer
reports that .apply is not idempotent.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pwm/pwm-sun8i.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pwm/pwm-sun8i.c b/drivers/pwm/pwm-sun8i.c
index 6e196f31314b..b07805ad7084 100644
--- a/drivers/pwm/pwm-sun8i.c
+++ b/drivers/pwm/pwm-sun8i.c
@@ -123,7 +123,7 @@ static int sun8i_pwm_get_state(struct pwm_chip *chip,
 				struct pwm_state *state)
 {
 	struct sun8i_pwm_chip *sun8i_chip = to_sun8i_pwm_chip(chip);
-	u16 ent_cycle, act_cycle, prescale_k;
+	u32 ent_cycle, act_cycle, prescale_k;
 	u64 clk_rate, tmp;
 	u8 div_m;
 	u32 val;
@@ -154,7 +154,8 @@ static int sun8i_pwm_get_state(struct pwm_chip *chip,
 	val = sun8i_pwm_readl(sun8i_chip, SUN8I_PWM_PERIOD(pwm->hwpwm));
 	act_cycle = FIELD_GET(SUN8I_PWM_PERIOD_ACT_CYCLE, val);
 
-	ent_cycle = FIELD_GET(SUN8I_PWM_PERIOD_ENTIRE_CYCLE, val);
+	/* For N cycles, PPRx.PWM_ENTIRE_CYCLE = (N-1) */
+	ent_cycle = FIELD_GET(SUN8I_PWM_PERIOD_ENTIRE_CYCLE, val) + 1;
 
 	/*
 	 * The duration of the active phase should not be longer
@@ -164,7 +165,7 @@ static int sun8i_pwm_get_state(struct pwm_chip *chip,
 		act_cycle = ent_cycle;
 
 	/*
-	 * We have act_cycle <= ent_cycle <= 0xffff, prescale_k <= 0x100,
+	 * We have act_cycle <= ent_cycle <= 0x10000, prescale_k <= 0x100,
 	 * div_m <= 8. So the multiplication fits into an u64 without
 	 * overflow.
 	 */
